    title: "Strength Training for Soccer: Hamstrings, Groin, and Repeat Sprints", seoTitle: "Soccer Strength Training Plan | DoThis",
    description: "A soccer strength plan built around the injuries that actually end seasons, with exact sets, reps, rest, and in-season scheduling.",
    published: "2026-08-06", modified: "2026-08-06", displayDate: "August 6, 2026", readingMinutes: 11,
    summary: "Hamstring and groin strains account for a large share of missed soccer time. A plan that ignores eccentric hamstring and adductor work is missing the point.",
    directAnswer: "Lift twice a week around training and matches. Include eccentric hamstring work and adductor loading every week without exception, and place heavy legs away from match day.",
    whoIntro: "This is for outfield players at any competitive level who train or play several times a week. Goalkeepers should keep the same lower body and add more overhead work.",
    forWhom: ["Players with a history of hamstring or groin strains.", "Anyone whose sprint speed fades in the last twenty minutes.", "Players returning from a layoff who need a re-entry structure.", "Adults playing recreationally who train less than they play."],
    scheduleIntro: "Lift on the day after a match or on a training day, never the day before a match. Two sessions is the realistic ceiling once matches and team training are on the calendar.",
    schedule: [{ day: "Day after match", plan: "Session A", purpose: "Heavy, furthest from the next match" }, { day: "Mid-week training day", plan: "Session B", purpose: "Shorter, after team training" }, { day: "Day before match", plan: "Nothing heavy", purpose: "Arrive fresh" }, { day: "Match day", plan: "Play", purpose: "The point of all of it" }],
    warmupIntro: "Warm up properly. Cold hamstrings and a sudden sprint is the classic mechanism for the injury this plan exists to prevent.", warmup: sharedWarmup,
    workoutHeading: "The soccer strength plan", workoutIntro: "The hamstring and adductor work is the non-negotiable part. If time runs out, cut something else.",
    sessions: [
      { name: "Session A - Heavy and eccentric", intro: "The main session. Hamstring work goes early while you are fresh enough to control it.", exercises: [r("Nordic Hamstring Curl", "3", "5 reps", "2 min", "Lower as slowly as you can control; catch with the hands. Soreness is expected in the first weeks."), r("Barbell Back Squat", "4", "5 reps", "3 min", "Control the descent and drive out without the hips shooting up first."), r("Copenhagen Plank", "3", "20 sec each side", "90 sec", "Build the adductor before it gets loaded in a tackle."), r("Romanian Deadlift", "3", "8 reps", "2 min", "Hips back, hamstrings loaded, back steady."), r("Side Plank", "2", "30 sec each side", "60 sec", "Hold the position rather than chasing the clock.")] },
      { name: "Session B - Single-leg and trunk", intro: "Shorter and lighter, fitted after team training.", exercises: [r("Bulgarian Split Squat", "3", "8 each side", "90 sec", "Soccer is played on one leg; train it that way."), r("Single-Leg Romanian Deadlift", "3", "8 each side", "90 sec", "Slow and balanced beats heavy and wobbling."), r("Hip Adduction", "3", "10-12 reps", "90 sec", "Second adductor exposure of the week."), r("Step-Up", "3", "8 each side", "90 sec", "Drive through the top leg without pushing off the bottom foot."), r("Dead Bug", "2", "8 each side", "60 sec", "Keep the ribs down.")] },
    ],
