    recovery: ["Expect two to three weeks of leg soreness when starting, then very little. Begin a lifting block in an easier riding week.", "Do not start lifting in the four weeks before a goal event.", "Upper-body work costs almost nothing in ride quality and can stay in year round."],
    faq: [{ question: "Will lifting make me heavier?", answer: "Two low-volume sessions a week build force well before size. Most cyclists gain little or no weight and hold power better late in efforts." }, { question: "Should I lift during race season?", answer: "One session a week at maintained loads keeps nearly everything and costs almost nothing." }, { question: "Why low reps?", answer: "Heavy low-rep work builds force with far less muscle damage than high-rep leg work, which means the next ride is unaffected." }],
    safety: "Stop if an exercise produces sharp pain, dizziness, or chest pain. Knee pain that appears on the bike after starting lifting usually means loads rose too quickly.",
