    progressionIntro: "Decide the ladder before you need it. This is what separates a bodyweight plan that progresses from one that plateaus at twenty push-ups.",
    progression: ["Push-ups: incline, then floor, then feet elevated, then one arm assisted.", "Squats: bodyweight, then split squat, then rear-foot-elevated, then one leg to a chair.", "Rows: feet on floor, then feet elevated, then one arm.", "Move up the ladder when every set hits the top of the range with clean technique, then restart at the bottom of the range in the harder variation.", "Slowing the lowering phase to three seconds is a legitimate half-step when the next variation is too big a jump."],
